<VI _name="pa_close_join.vi" description="M-CLOSE helper\3A rewires an Actor Core override that has a helper-loop branch (top level\2C found by VI name)\2C Call Parent and a one-frame Flat Sequence holding the stop hook (found by VI name) into the close shape\3A (1) a NEW close subVI on the top level (path)\2C its class input from the loop's class net\2C its error in from a NEW Merge Errors A (loop error out\2C stop hook error out\3B the latter leaves the frame through a new tunnel)\3B (2) the override's error out indicator from a NEW Merge Errors B (Call Parent error out\2C close error out)\3B Call Parent's whole error-out net is deleted (its old order tunnel then vanishes\2C LabVIEW drops a tunnel with no wire on either side) and rebuilt\3A Merge B first input\2C then a new order tunnel made by wiring Call Parent error out to the stop hook's error in and deleting that inner wire (05 rule 77\3B a tunnel with its outer wire stays). Optionally deletes one more subVI in the frame (remove vi regex)\3B that Delete is outside the error chain and reports only to delete node error (1055 there = nothing matched\2C the default)\2C so the steps after it run either way. Then runs Remove Bad Wires. The stop hook's and close's error input is found as error in or error in (no error). Merge Errors is created by New VI Object (vi object class GrowableFunction\2C style 2147 = palette id BI2147\3B class Function answers 1057\3B the new node reads Class Name Bundler\2C Style Merge Errors). Inputs are found by Is Source? = F in pane order. Saves VI and class. Project OPEN and ACTIVE.">
